\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Arc precisions and finite-range symbols}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{A [cyclic arc precision](fdip-00B6) assigns a matrix to
every finite subset of the [dyadic index](fdip-00B6). The
data are the cyclic order and the lengths of the arcs. A
[finite-range circle precision](fdip-00C8) assigns another
matrix to the residues modulo #{N}. Its symbol has finite
range, the second-order coefficient is #{\kappa}, and the
mass #{\mu} stands on the diagonal. A negative coefficient
#{c_r} remains in that definition whenever #{\kappa>0} and
the symbol is positive away from multiples of #{2\pi}.}

\p{Decimation selects one nearest-neighbor shape
(\ref{fdip-00AY}). The second moment of a coordinate
difference is computed from the two-point law. The metric
completion of that moment comes before the comparison with
the covariance of \ref{fdip-00BG}.}
